(PRC-22 — `Create a device node called "<path>" with type "c" major N
 minor M.` performs mknod(2).
 Also covers: PRC-23 (type "b" is accepted), PRC-25 (major/minor are the
 standard Linux device numbers — 1:3 is /dev/null, 7:0 is /dev/loop0) and
 PRC-26 (the error flag is set on failure).
 SAFETY: creating a CHARACTER or BLOCK device node needs CAP_MKNOD, so
 both calls return EPERM here and nothing appears on disk — the probe
 checks that. Type "p" is the exception and really does create something;
 see D1.vox.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-22.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the character device node set the error flag
   the block device node set the error flag
   no character node was created
   no block node was created
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
Create a device node called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_null" with type "c" major 1 minor 3.
On error print "the character device node set the error flag".
Create a device node called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_loop" with type "b" major 7 minor 0.
On error print "the block device node set the error flag".
If "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_null" is not available then, print "no character node was created".
If "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_loop" is not available then, print "no block node was created".
